#: ../../source/docs/copter-adding-custom-controller.rst:90
#: 78b2d6db30a54c528ca7e2a33f561017
msgid "The PID controller backend has the same controller architecture as the main controller. It doesn't have any safeguarding mechanism such as acceleration limiting or rate limiting. The default gains are scaled 0.9 times to differentiate the custom controller response from the main one. Since this controller does not have acceleration limiting, specifically a square root controller, it would be safer to give a gentle command while flying with it. Although it has the same architecture as the main one, a proper reset functionality is not implemented intentionally to make it easier to detect the effect of improper resetting."
msgstr ""

